---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PolicyContact from "../components/PolicyContact.astro";
import { THEME_STORAGE_KEY } from "../lib/keys";
import { LEGAL_HOLDER } from "../data/site";
---

<Layout
  title="The Bead Reserve : Privacy"
  description="What The Bead Reserve's website collects and what it keeps in the browser."
>
  <main>
    <article class="policy bracket-frame">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Last updated: October 8, 2026</p>
        <p>
          This policy describes what information The Bead Reserve website, owned
          by {LEGAL_HOLDER} (a California LLC), collects and what happens to it.
          The site has no accounts. It collects very little.
        </p>

        <h2>What this site collects</h2>
        <p>
          The site is hosted by
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/">Cloudflare</a>. Like nearly
          every host, Cloudflare may keep standard request logs (your IP address
          and the pages you request) as part of serving the site.
        </p>
        <p>
          The camera frames and reserve status on the home page are served by
          the reserve's own Worker, at <code>/api/</code> on this domain.
          Requests for them are ordinary requests to this site, and the
          paragraph above covers them.
        </p>
        <p>
          This site uses
          <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/"
            >Cloudflare Web Analytics</a
          >
          to count page views. Cloudflare adds a small script to each page for
          this. It sets no cookies, stores nothing in your browser, and does not
          follow you to other sites. It produces a tally of which pages were
          read.
        </p>
        <p>
          The typefaces are served from this site. Your browser requests no font
          from a third party.
        </p>
        <p>
          Claiming and redeeming BEADZ connect a wallet to the site. The site
          reads your wallet's public address to show its holdings and to submit
          the transaction you approve. I do not store the address. Transactions
          on Base are public and permanent. I can neither hide nor remove them.
        </p>
        <p>
          A redemption is delivered by certified mail, which requires a name and
          a postal address. I collect these at redemption, use them to address
          that shipment and nothing else, and delete them once delivery is
          confirmed.
        </p>

        <h2 id="cookies-and-browser-storage">Cookies and browser storage</h2>
        <p>
          The site sets no cookies of its own. Cloudflare runs bot protection in
          front of the site, and that sets one cookie, <code>cf_clearance</code
          >. It tells Cloudflare your browser already passed its check, so you
          don't get challenged again. It lasts up to a year and only Cloudflare
          can read it. It isn't used for ads or to follow you around the web.
        </p>
        <p>
          The site also keeps two small values in your browser's local storage.
          Neither is sent anywhere and neither identifies you.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <code>{THEME_STORAGE_KEY}</code>: your light or dark theme choice,
            saved when you use the toggle.
          </li>
          <li>
            <code>half-built-ecosystem</code>: a copy of the list of my other
            sites shown in the footer, kept for a day so it isn't fetched on
            every page. The list comes from ecosystem.half-built-robots.com,
            which is also mine and also on Cloudflare.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>Clearing your browser's data for this site removes both.</p>

        <h2>Do Not Track</h2>
        <p>
          Nothing on this site tracks you across other sites, so it behaves the
          same whether or not your browser sends a Do Not Track or Global
          Privacy Control signal. There is nothing for the signal to turn off.
        </p>

        <h2>Mailing list</h2>
        <p>
          The signup form on the home page subscribes you to the Half-Built
          Robots mailing list, the same list the blog runs. If you subscribe,
          the email address you provide is used to send you the newsletter and
          nothing else. It is not sold or shared. Addresses are stored and mail
          is sent by <a href="https://buttondown.com/">Buttondown</a>. Signup is
          double opt-in. You can leave at any time using the unsubscribe link at
          the bottom of every email, or by asking using the contact information
          below. The details are in the blog's
          <a href="https://www.half-built-robots.com/policies/mailing-list/"
            >mailing list policy</a
          >.
        </p>

        <h2>Why it's kept and for how long</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Mailing list address.</strong> You signed up and confirmed
            by email, so it's held on your consent. It's kept until you
            unsubscribe.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Redemption shipping details.</strong> Held until delivery is
            confirmed, then deleted.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Cloudflare's logs, analytics, and bot protection.</strong>
            These keep the site running and protected. Cloudflare keeps them on
            its own schedule under
            <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
              >Cloudflare's privacy policy</a
            >.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Email you send me.</strong> It's used to answer you, and it
            stays in my inbox unless you ask me to delete it.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Where it's processed</h2>
        <p>
          Cloudflare, Buttondown, and Google are United States companies, so
          anything they hold for this site is processed in the US. Cloudflare
          takes part in the EU-US Data Privacy Framework.
        </p>

        <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
        <p>
          The site links to the Half-Built Robots blog and to other sites. Their
          privacy practices are their own. This policy covers only this site.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          This site is not directed at children under 13, and I do not knowingly
          collect personal information from anyone under 13.
        </p>

        <h2>Your data</h2>
        <p>
          Wherever you live, you can ask what this site holds about you. You can
          also ask to have it corrected or deleted. Write to the contact address
          below. In nearly every case the site holds nothing. The records it can
          hold are a mailing list address and, while a redemption is in transit,
          a shipping address. The unsubscribe link in any email removes the
          first.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you think a request was handled badly, you can complain to the data
          protection authority where you live.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          Updates to this policy are posted on this page with a new date at the
          top.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <PolicyContact />
        <p>
          The email address is a Gmail account, so mail sent to it is also
          handled by Google under
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
            >Google's privacy policy</a
          >.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
